IMPORT prelude

-- Community Mediation Centres Act 1997 (Singapore) -- which disputes a person may bring for mediation and who must consent
-- (ss 9(3), 11(1)), who may sit in (s 10(5)), when attendance is voluntary (s 12), when a settlement binds (s 13(2)), who may
-- speak for a party (s 14), referral by a Magistrate (s 15(1)), how long records are kept (s 7(2)), immunity of mediators
-- (s 17), court orders against the Centre (s 18(1)), defamation privilege and the exclusion of what was said (s 19), and when
-- a mediator may disclose information (s 20).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CMCA1997.txt. Its cover says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021"; the body also shows later amendments annotated "[Act 25 of 2021 wef
-- 01/04/2022]" (s 18) and "[Act 43 of 2024 wef 24/03/2025]" (ss 9(3), 12(2A), 14(1A), 15(2), 15B). The deposit's metadata
-- calls it the "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026". The body numbers the sections 20 Secrecy, 21 [Repealed], 22 Public
-- servants, 23 Regulations; the arrangement at the top is one line out of step with that. The body's numbering is followed.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance (Tier 1): Community Mediation Centres are where neighbour, family and
-- community quarrels are sent, by the parties themselves or by a Magistrate or tribunal. SCOPED to the provisions a party meets.
-- Not encoded: establishment, Directors and delegation (ss 3-6), appointment and pay of mediators (s 8), the conduct rules of
-- s 10(1)-(4) beyond a comment, the outcome-reporting duties of ss 15(3), 15A(1)(b), 15B, evaluation (s 16), s 17(2), the
-- public-servant deeming (s 22) and regulations (s 23). The cross-referenced Acts (Criminal Procedure Code 2010, Small Claims
-- Tribunals Act 1984, Community Disputes Resolution Act 2015) were not read.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Community Mediation Centres Act 1997 -- mediation`

DECLARE DisputeKind IS ONE OF
    `a family dispute`
    `a social dispute`
    `a community dispute`
    `a commercial debt claim`

DECLARE Route IS ONE OF
    `the parties' own application`
    `a Magistrate's referral under s 15`
    `a Small Claims Tribunal referral under SCTA s 18A`
    `a CDRA s 13M referral`
    `a CDRA s 30 referral`

§§ `9(3) and 11(1) -- which disputes come in`

-- s 11(1): "Subject to sections 9(3), 15 and 15A and the Community Disputes Resolution Act 2015, any person may refer to a
-- mediator ... a case concerning a family, social or community dispute that does not involve a seizable offence under any
-- written law."
-- s 9(3): "Subject to sections 15, 15A and 15B and the Community Disputes Resolution Act 2015, a dispute must not be accepted
-- for mediation except with the consent of the Director ... who may decline to consent".
-- s 11(2): mediation may proceed "whether or not the dispute is justiciable" and whether or not it is the subject of legal
-- proceedings.
-- INFERENCE: the "subject to" words are read as meaning that a referral under s 15, 15A or 15B (or the CDRA) does not need
-- the Director's consent or the s 11(1) subject-matter test. The text does not say so in terms. A commercial debt claim is
-- treated as outside "family, social or community"; the Act does not define those words.
GIVEN `the kind` IS A DisputeKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the kind is family, social or community` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a commercial debt claim` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the route` IS A Route
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the route is a compulsory referral` IF
    CONSIDER `the route`
    WHEN `the parties' own application` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the route` IS A Route, `the kind` IS A DisputeKind, `involves a seizable offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Director consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dispute may be accepted for mediation` IF
        `the route is a compulsory referral` `the route`
    OR  (    `the kind is family, social or community` `the kind`
         AND (NOT `involves a seizable offence`)
         AND `the Director consents`)

§§ `10(5) -- who may be present`

-- s 10(5): "A mediation session must be conducted in the absence of the public, but persons who are not parties ... may, with
-- the permission of the Director and the parties, be present at or participate". (s 10(3): the rules of evidence do not apply;
-- s 10(4): a dispute "may not be adjudicated or arbitrated upon" at a session.)
GIVEN `the Director permits` IS A BOOLEAN, `the parties permit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a non-party may be present` IF
    `the Director permits` AND `the parties permit`

§§ `12 -- voluntary, except on referral`

-- s 12(1): "Attendance at and participation in a mediation session is voluntary." (2): a party "may withdraw ... at any time".
-- (2A): (1) and (2) "do not apply" to a session that takes place because of a referral under s 15, CDRA s 13M or 30, or SCTA
-- s 18A [Act 43 of 2024 wef 24/03/2025]. (3): attending or withdrawing "does not affect any rights or remedies" apart from the
-- Act. s 9(4): the mediator or the Director may terminate a session at any time.
GIVEN `the route` IS A Route
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `attendance is voluntary` IF
    NOT `the route is a compulsory referral` `the route`

GIVEN `the route` IS A Route
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a party may withdraw at any time` IF
    NOT `the route is a compulsory referral` `the route`

§§ `13 -- when a settlement binds`

-- s 13(1): terms "must, if the mediator thinks fit, be reduced to writing and signed". (2): "No settlement or agreement is
-- binding on the parties ... unless it has been reduced to writing with a statement signed by or on behalf of the parties to
-- this effect." An oral agreement at the session binds no one under this section.
GIVEN `reduced to writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `signed statement that it binds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the settlement is binding` IF
    `reduced to writing` AND `signed statement that it binds`

§§ `14 -- representation by an agent`

-- s 14(1): a party "is not entitled to be represented by an agent unless" (a) it appears to the Director that (i) an agent
-- should be permitted to facilitate mediation and (ii) the agent has sufficient knowledge of the matter, and (b) the Director so
-- approves. (1A) [Act 43 of 2024]: for a mediation mentioned in s 12(2A), the Director "must not approve" unless (a) the party
-- authorises the agent IN WRITING to represent it and to agree terms on its behalf, and (b) the agent signifies IN WRITING
-- willingness to act. (3): approval may carry conditions. (4): s 14 "does not apply to a claim referred ... under section 18A of
-- the Small Claims Tribunals Act 1984" (s 15A(1)(a) points instead to SCTA s 23(2), not read).
GIVEN `the route` IS A Route
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 14 governs representation` IF
    CONSIDER `the route`
    WHEN `a Small Claims Tribunal referral under SCTA s 18A` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the route` IS A Route,
      `an agent would facilitate mediation` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the agent knows the matter sufficiently` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Director approves` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the party authorised the agent in writing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the agent agreed in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agent may represent the party` IF
        `section 14 governs representation` `the route`
    AND `an agent would facilitate mediation`
    AND `the agent knows the matter sufficiently`
    AND `the Director approves`
    AND (    (NOT `the route is a compulsory referral` `the route`)
         OR  (`the party authorised the agent in writing` AND `the agent agreed in writing`))

-- s 14(2): s 14(1) does not prevent an officer of a body corporate, a council or committee member or managing agent of a strata
-- management corporation (Land Titles (Strata) Act 1967 s 10A), an officer of a statutory body, or an officer of a registered
-- society, "from representing" it. No such carve-out exists for an individual party.
DECLARE PartyKind IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a company`
    `a strata management corporation`
    `a statutory body`
    `a registered society`

GIVEN `the party` IS A PartyKind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an officer may represent the party without approval` IF
    CONSIDER `the party`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `15(1) -- referral by a Magistrate`

-- s 15(1): "Despite any provision of this Act or any written law, a Magistrate who receives a complaint made by a private person
-- under section 151 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 may, if (a) the offence is one for which a summons must ordinarily issue
-- in the first instance ... and (b) the Magistrate is of the opinion ... that the matter may more appropriately be resolved by
-- mediation, refer the complaint ... with or without the consent of both the complainant and the person complained against."
-- (2): the Magistrate may order either to attend, in person or by a representative permitted under s 14.
GIVEN `a private person's complaint under CPC s 151` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a summons offence in the first instance` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Magistrate thinks mediation more appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the complainant consents` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the person complained against consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Magistrate may refer the complaint` IF
        `a private person's complaint under CPC s 151`
    AND `a summons offence in the first instance`
    AND `the Magistrate thinks mediation more appropriate`

§§ `7(2) -- records`

-- s 7(2): records relating to a dispute "must be kept for a period of 3 years after the date the dispute is settled ..., or the
-- date of withdrawal from or termination of the mediation". Counted here in whole months after that date (36 months);
-- reading the period as ending exactly at 36 months is the encoder's.
GIVEN `months since settlement, withdrawal or termination` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the records must still be kept` IF
    `months since settlement, withdrawal or termination` LESS THAN 36

§§ `17(1) -- immunity`

-- s 17(1): nothing done or omitted by a mediator, Director or staff "shall, if the matter or thing was done in good faith for the
-- purpose of executing the provisions of this Act and did not involve any fraud or wilful misconduct, subject any of them to any
-- action, liability, claim or demand."
GIVEN `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN, `for the purpose of executing the Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `involved fraud` IS A BOOLEAN, `involved wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mediator is immune from suit` IF
        `in good faith`
    AND `for the purpose of executing the Act`
    AND (NOT `involved fraud`)
    AND (NOT `involved wilful misconduct`)

§§ `18(1) -- orders against the Centre in later litigation`

-- s 18(1): a registrar "must not" order the mediator, Director or staff to attend court, or order the Centre's records produced,
-- in proceedings connected with a referred dispute, "unless the registrar is satisfied that ... the attendance or production is
-- necessary for the fair disposal of the case or to save costs". (3): "court" includes an arbitral tribunal. (2): certified
-- copies suffice, admissible "subject to section 19".
GIVEN `necessary for fair disposal` IS A BOOLEAN, `necessary to save costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the registrar may order the mediator to attend` IF
    `necessary for fair disposal` OR `necessary to save costs`

§§ `19 -- privilege and inadmissibility`

-- s 19(1): the defamation privilege of judicial proceedings attaches to (a) a mediation session and (b) a document sent to or
-- produced at a Centre to arrange a session. (2): it "does not extend to a publication made otherwise than" (a) at a session,
-- (b) under (1)(b), or (c) as provided by s 20. (6): "mediation session" includes steps in arranging it and in its follow-up.
DECLARE Publication IS ONE OF
    `words spoken at the mediation session`
    `a letter sent to the Centre to arrange a session`
    `a disclosure made under section 20`
    `a post on social media about the other party`
    `a complaint to the other party's employer`

GIVEN `the publication` IS A Publication
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the publication is privileged from defamation` IF
    CONSIDER `the publication`
    WHEN `a post on social media about the other party` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a complaint to the other party's employer` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 19(3): "Evidence of anything said or of any admission made in a mediation session is not admissible in any proceedings
-- before any court, tribunal or body." (4): likewise a document prepared for or in the course of a session. (5): (3) and (4) do
-- not apply (a) where the persons in attendance or named (and, for a document, all persons named in it) consent; (b) in
-- proceedings about an act or omission disclosed under s 20(c); or (c) if the court is satisfied admission "is necessary for
-- the fair disposal of the case or to save costs".
GIVEN `everyone present or named consents` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proceedings about a section 20(c) disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the court finds it necessary for fair disposal or to save costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `what was said at mediation is admissible` IF
        `everyone present or named consents`
    OR  `proceedings about a section 20(c) disclosure`
    OR  `the court finds it necessary for fair disposal or to save costs`

§§ `20 -- secrecy`

-- s 20: a mediator, Director, staff member, evaluator or researcher "may disclose information obtained in connection with the
-- administration or execution of this Act only as follows": (a) with the consent of the person it came from; (b) in connection
-- with the administration or execution of the Act; (c) "where there are reasonable grounds to believe that disclosure is
-- necessary to prevent or minimise the danger of injury to any person or damage to any property"; (d) to refer parties to an
-- agency, with the parties' consent; (e) for research or evaluation, without revealing identity without consent; (f) by court
-- order or under written law. s 20 itself states no penalty; none is encoded.
DECLARE DisclosureGround IS ONE OF
    `the source of the information consents`
    `administering the Act`
    `reasonable belief it prevents injury or property damage`
    `referring the parties to an agency with their consent`
    `anonymised research approved by the Director`
    `research naming a party without consent`
    `a court order`
    `a journalist's request`
    `the other party's request`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A DisclosureGround
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the mediator may disclose` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `research naming a party without consent` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a journalist's request` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the other party's request` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
